      <div type="clause" n="9.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 9.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="9.2" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="54" ed="#liebermann"/>Geo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.star2"/> wæs goldðeofe ⁊ stodðeofe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="49" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.49"/> ⁊ beoðeofe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="49" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.49"/>, ⁊ manig witu maran ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> oþru; nu sint<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="50" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.50"/> eal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="51" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.51"/> gelic buton manðeofe:<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="49" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.49"/> CXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="52" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.52"/> scill’.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="9.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="54" ed="#liebermann"/>Geo wæs goldþeofe ⁊ stodþeofe ⁊ beoþeofe, ⁊ monegu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.1"/> witu maran ðonne oþru; nu sint eall<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.15"/> gelic buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.1"/> monþeofe:<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.16"/> CXX scll'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="9.2" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="55" ed="#liebermann"/>Hwilon wæs goldþeofe ⁊ stodðeowe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.4"/> [⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.5"/> beoþeofe,] ⁊ manig wítu maran þonne oðru; nu synd ealle gelice, butan manþeofe:<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.6-2"/> hundtwelftig scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="9.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="55" ed="#liebermann"/>Aliquando fuit de eo qui aurum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.18"/> furabatur uel equas siluestres uel apes, et multe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.19"/> wite maiores<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.20"/> quam alie. Nunc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.21"/> sunt omnes pares<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.6"/> preter manþeofe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.22"/> (qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.oe.23"/> hominem furatur): centum uiginti sol.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="68–70" ed="#attenborough"/>Geo<ptr type="editorNote" n="20" target="#Af_9-2.attnote.fn.20"/> was goldðeofe ⁊ stódðeofe<ptr type="editorNote" n="21" target="#Af_9-2.attnote.fn.21"/> ⁊ beoðeofe, ⁊ manig<ptr type="editorNote" n="22" target="#Af_9-2.attnote.fn.22"/> witu maran ðonne oþru; nu sint<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_9-2.attnote.fn.1"/> eal gelic buton manðeofe: CXX scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="11.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="304" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Geo wæs goldðeofe ⁊ stódðeofe ⁊ beoðeofe, ⁊ manig witu maran ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> oþru; nu sint eal gelic buton manðeofe: CXX scill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="55" ed="#liebermann"/>Einst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.de.1"/> war dem Golddiebe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.de.2"/> und Gestütsdiebe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.de.3"/> und Bienendiebe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.de.4"/> [je eine Strafe], und viele [Missethaten hatten] Strafgelder grösser als andere; jetzt sind alle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.de.5"/> gleich, ausser Menschendieb:<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_9-2.lnote.de.6"/> 120 Schill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Formerly there was [a separate fine] for the gold-thief and the stud-thief and the bee-thief, and many [offences had] fines greater than others; now all are equal, except the man-thief: 120 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="69" ed="#attenborough"/>Formerly the fines to be paid by those who stole gold and horses and bees, and many other fines, were greater than the rest. Now all fines, with the exception of that for stealing men, are alike—120 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="412" ed="#whitelock"/>Formerly, [the fine] for the stealer of gold, the stealer of stud-horses, the stealer of bees, and many fines, were greater than others; now all are alike, except for the stealer of a man: 120 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="305" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Earlier the fines for a gold-thief and a stud-thief and a bee-thief and many fines were greater than others; now all are alike except theft of a person:120 shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="278"><label>contradicts</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_7">Ine 7</ref> <quote>where Ine called sixty shillings the 'full fine' with evident reference to theft, Alfred stipulated that 120 shillings was to be the fine for all thefts (n. 72)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="278"><label>contradicts</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_10">Ine 10</ref> <quote>where Ine called sixty shillings the 'full fine' with evident reference to theft, Alfred stipulated that 120 shillings was to be the fine for all thefts (n. 72)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="278"><label>contradicts</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_43">Ine 43</ref> <quote>where Ine called sixty shillings the 'full fine' with evident reference to theft, Alfred stipulated that 120 shillings was to be the fine for all thefts (n. 72)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="278"><label>contradicts</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_46">Ine 46</ref> <quote>where Ine called sixty shillings the 'full fine' with evident reference to theft, Alfred stipulated that 120 shillings was to be the fine for all thefts (n. 72)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="305"><ref target="clause:IIAs_1">II As 1–1.5</ref></note>
