        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_9-2.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> mann.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to mann.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B modernisiert. — Bewusste Abschaffung <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Gesetz 22</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B modernises. — Deliberate abolition: see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Gesetz 22</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘gab es Golddiebe’. Der Dativ <hi rend="italic">þeofe</hi> erklärt sich wie der hinter ‘gehören, zukommen’ (Mätzner <hi rend="italic">Engl. Gramm.</hi> II 191); ‘Strafe’ ist ergänzbar aus dem folg. Plural. — Oder aber <hi rend="italic">-þeofe</hi> bed. hier viermal nom. -‘Diebstahl’ (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7a), und es ist zu übs.: ‘einst gab es Golddiebstahl .... ausser Menschendiebstahl’; denn ein fem. <hi rend="italic">þeofe, þiefe</hi> belegt <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> und Toller. — <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gold 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘there were gold-thieves’. The dative <hi rend="italic">þeofe</hi> is to be explained like the dative after ‘belong to, be due to’ (Mätzner <hi rend="italic">Engl. Gramm.</hi> II 191); ‘penalty’ can be supplied from the following plural. — Alternatively, <hi rend="italic">-þeofe</hi> here, all four times, means nom. -‘theft’ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7a), and the translation should be: ‘formerly there was gold-theft .... except man-theft’; for a fem. <hi rend="italic">þeofe, þiefe</hi> is attested by <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> and Toller. — <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gold 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘Hengst’ oder ‘Stute’, sondern ‘Pferdeherde’; Toller. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Pferd 4. 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘stallion’ or ‘mare’, but ‘herd of horses’; Toller. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Pferd 4. 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Bienen 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Bienen 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ergänze ‘Strafen’ laut der neutr. Form, nicht ‘Diebe’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Supply ‘penalties’, in accordance with the neuter form, not ‘thieves’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_9-2.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">53</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Lond bietet wieder Q’s ältere Lesung. — Da der Zusammenhang Fahrnisdiebstahl, nicht Freiheitsberaubung behandelt, ist <hi rend="italic">man</hi> ein Unfreier; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Menschenraub 1. 2a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Lond again offers Q’s older reading. — Since the context deals with theft of chattels, not deprivation of liberty, <hi rend="italic">man</hi> is an unfree person; see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Menschenraub 1. 2a</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_9-2.attnote.fn.20" n="20" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><label>Geo</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Hwilon</hi>. B &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_9-2.attnote.fn.21" n="21" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><label>stódðeofe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">stodðeowe</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_9-2.attnote.fn.22" n="22" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">68</biblScope></bibl><label>manig</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">manegu</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_9-2.attnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope></bibl><label>sint</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">synd</hi>. B &amp; Ld.</seg></note>
